+/// (`0016:355-356`: the published parts "**and/or**" a rolled-back attempt's dangling segments).
+///
+/// Walked in lockstep — one `outer` counter serving both — the walk stops at the first *joint*
+/// gap: a sparse part set whose numbers do not line up with the segment indices ends the
+/// obligation with part records still naming durable bytes, and the obligation deleted on top.
+/// The writer of this shape is #625's rollback, so the test is the writer here.
